      "tool": "open_pr",
      "args": {
        "title": "Fix register_hook to extend list when hook argument is a list",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nWhen passing a list of hooks via `hooks={\"response\": [f1, f2]}` or calling `register_hook(\"response\", [f1, f2])`, the entire list was being appended as a single item rather than each callable being added individually. This caused items in the hook list to be non-callable (the list itself was the item).\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `src/requests/models.py`, updated `register_hook` to check if the `hook` argument is a list. If it is, use `extend` to add each callable individually; otherwise, use `append` as before.\n\n```python\ndef register_hook(self, event, hook):\n    \"\"\"Properly register a hook.\"\"\"\n    if isinstance(hook, list):\n        self.hooks[event].extend(hook)\n    else:\n        self.hooks[event].append(hook)\n```\n\n## Testing\n\nThe fix passes `tests/test_requests.py::test_allow_list_of_hooks_to_register_hook`."
      },
